    <briefdescription>
<para>A clock implementation for Terrestrial Time (TT). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Terrestrial Time is a continuous time scale defined by the IAU. It is related to International Atomic Time (TAI) by a fixed offset: TT = TAI + 32.184 seconds. TT is commonly used in astrodynamics as the independent variable for planetary motion equations.</para>
<para>This clock provides conversions to and from the system clock via the TAI clock, accounting for the fixed TT-TAI offset. Leap seconds are handled transparently through std::chrono::tai_clock. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
